        min_points=2,
        model_answer="The neutral wire is kept at or near 0 V, the potential of the ground, so there is very little potential difference between it and a person standing on the floor and only a small current could flow. The live wire alternates to about 230 V, so a large p.d. between it and the ground drives a dangerous current through anyone touching it. However, the neutral wire carries the circuit current and may not be at exactly 0 V, especially if there is a fault, so neither wire should ever be touched.",
