        model_answer="Keep the appliances, their plugs and your hands dry, and never use them with wet hands or where they could fall into the sink, because water conducts and lowers the body's resistance, increasing shock current. Do not run the kettle, toaster and microwave from one socket or extension lead at the same time, because their currents add and the cable could overheat and start a fire. Check that cables are not frayed and that each plug has the correct fuse and, for metal-cased appliances, an earth connection, so that a fault blows the fuse instead of making the casing live.",
